# AATPE sepolicy.rule -- OPTIONAL static SELinux fallback.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normally AATPE applies its eBPF/perf_event permissions at RUNTIME from
# post-fs-data.sh via `magiskpolicy --live` (Magisk) / `supolicy --live` (KSU).
# That live path already covers the domains the daemon actually runs in.
#
# ONLY drop the lines below (remove the leading '#') if:
#   - your ROM ships WITHOUT magiskpolicy / supolicy (so the live path can't run), AND
#   - you see "avc: denied ... bpf / perf_event" in logcat, AND
#   - eBPF remains disabled (state/ebpf_active != 1) despite correct setup.
#
# Rules are intentionally minimal (self-domain only), matching the live policy.
# enable one block for your loader:
#
# --- Magisk (daemon runs in the magisk domain) ---
# allow magisk self bpf { map_create prog_load map_read map_write }
# allow magisk self perf_event { open read write ioctl }
#
# --- KernelSU (daemon may run in init or su domain) ---
# allow init init bpf { map_create prog_load map_read map_write }
# allow init init perf_event { open read write ioctl }
# allow su   su   bpf { map_create prog_load map_read map_write }
# allow su   su   perf_event { open read write ioctl }
#
# --- APatch (uses magiskpolicy / magisk domain) ---
# allow magisk magisk bpf { map_create prog_load map_read map_write }
# allow magisk magisk perf_event { open read write ioctl }
